1
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:04,940
Hey, want to spend some time

2
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:06,680
playing the new Star Wars game this weekend?

3
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:07,530
Oh, I don't know.

4
00:00:07,530 --> 00:00:09,960
I kind of promised myself I'd get off the computer,

5
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:12,750
be more physically active. Get some exercise...

6
00:00:12,770 --> 00:00:15,170
You're about to walk up three flights of stairs.

7
00:00:17,580 --> 00:00:18,990
Good point, I'm in.

8
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:22,330
You know what would be great?

9
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:24,040
Let's do it like the old days.

10
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:25,900
You mean, are you talking gaming marathon?

11
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:27,720
Yeah. Start Saturday morning,

12
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:29,080
go 48 hours,

13
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:31,010
sleeping bags, junk food...

14
00:00:31,010 --> 00:00:33,950
Turn off our phones so our moms can't call.

15
00:00:35,970 --> 00:00:38,190
It would be like our World Of Warcraft a few years ago

16
00:00:38,190 --> 00:00:40,490
when the neighbors called the cops on us.

17
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:43,040
They called the cops because of the smell.

18
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:44,640
They thought we were dead.

19
00:00:47,430 --> 00:00:49,910
We were badass back in the day.

20
00:00:52,270 --> 00:00:53,420
All right, let's do it.

21
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:55,510
48 hours of Star Wars gaming.

22
00:00:55,510 --> 00:00:57,800
It's on like Alderaan.

23
00:01:00,130 --> 00:01:01,740
Hey, Sheldon, clear your weekend.

24
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:04,530
Starting Saturday morning, Star Wars marathon.

25
00:01:04,530 --> 00:01:06,160
Movies or video games?

26
00:01:06,160 --> 00:01:07,060
No, board game?

27
00:01:07,060 --> 00:01:08,300
Or trading card games?

28
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:09,860
Or Lego's? Or dress up?

29
00:01:09,870 --> 00:01:10,800
Or comic books?!

30
00:01:10,810 --> 00:01:12,710
Or dramatic readings of Novelizations?!

31
00:01:12,710 --> 00:01:14,200
Yes to all!

32
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:18,700
We are going to play the online game.

33
00:01:18,700 --> 00:01:20,370
The online game?!

34
00:01:20,370 --> 00:01:21,520
Bully!

35
00:01:22,950 --> 00:01:25,040
Gentlemen, as much as I'm sure Sheldon would enjoy

36
00:01:25,050 --> 00:01:26,730
playing intergalactic make-believe,

37
00:01:26,730 --> 00:01:27,970
he and I have other plans.

38
00:01:27,970 --> 00:01:31,090
We are attending my Aunt Flora's 93rd birthday party.

39
00:01:31,560 --> 00:01:33,510
Just tell her I can't come.

40
00:01:33,830 --> 00:01:35,920
She'll be disappointed if we don't show up.

41
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:37,220
She's 93.

42
00:01:37,230 --> 00:01:39,480
She won't be disappointed for very long.

43
00:01:41,180 --> 00:01:43,580
No, hang on. I followed all the protocols

44
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:45,850
set forth by you in the relationship agreement.

45
00:01:45,850 --> 00:01:48,940
I made a written record request 72 hours in advance.

46
00:01:49,850 --> 00:01:51,900
I checked the tire pressure on the car.

47
00:01:52,220 --> 00:01:54,590
I even contacted the Centers For Disease Control to find out

48
00:01:54,590 --> 00:01:57,360
what shots they recommend for travel to Orange County.

49
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:00,840
FYI, it's none.

50
00:02:02,130 --> 00:02:04,600
Amy, the relationship agreement was not designed

51
00:02:04,600 --> 00:02:06,850
for either one of us to get our way.

52
00:02:07,290 --> 00:02:08,740
You use it to get your way.

53
00:02:08,740 --> 00:02:10,960
I use it to get the right way.

54
00:02:12,060 --> 00:02:14,490
The fact that the right way is also my way

55
00:02:14,490 --> 00:02:16,240
is a happy coincidence.

56
00:02:17,380 --> 00:02:18,500
You gave me your word.

57
00:02:18,500 --> 00:02:20,020
You're coming with me.

58
00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:21,530
We'll miss you, Sheldon.

59
00:02:21,570 --> 00:02:22,900
Yeah, well,

60
00:02:22,900 --> 00:02:24,400
who wants to spend the whole weekend,

61
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:25,950
running around a bunch of pretend planets

62
00:02:25,950 --> 00:02:27,490
battling made up monsters.

63
00:02:27,490 --> 00:02:29,140
That's for babies.

64
00:02:30,160 --> 00:02:31,480
Yeah, but it's got lightsabers.

65
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:34,380
Yeah, please, Amy! It's got lightsabers!

66
00:03:01,610 --> 00:03:02,500
Hello, Stewart.

67
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:03,590
Hey, Sheldon.

68
00:03:03,590 --> 00:03:04,760
Help you with anything?

69
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:07,420
Yes, I'm attending a party this weekend

70
00:03:07,420 --> 00:03:09,630
for a 93-year-old woman.

71
00:03:10,690 --> 00:03:12,530
Can you recommend a gift?

72
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:15,120
Uh, I don't know.

73
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:18,460
Could put a tennis ball on the end of Excalibur.

74
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:21,010
Make a pretty badass cane.

75
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:24,080
- Do you supply the tennis ball?  - No.

76
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:25,260
Then no.

77
00:03:27,130 --> 00:03:28,340
What else?

78
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:33,390
Oh, have this collectors edition batman utility belt.

79
00:03:33,390 --> 00:03:37,090
Maybe she can use it as a wearable pill caddy.

80
00:03:38,490 --> 00:03:40,540
Well, she'd just look silly wearing that

81
00:03:40,540 --> 00:03:42,700
without the rest of the costume.

82
00:03:45,070 --> 00:03:47,360
I'm sorry Sheldon, that's it. That's all I got.

83
00:03:47,370 --> 00:03:48,700
Oh, it's not your fault.

84
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:50,290
I've been to the model train store.

85
00:03:50,290 --> 00:03:51,730
I've been to Radio Shack.

86
00:03:51,730 --> 00:03:54,250
This woman is impossible to shop for.

87
00:03:55,330 --> 00:03:57,280
I'd make fun of Sheldon for having girl problems

88
00:03:57,280 --> 00:04:01,040
if I wasn't in shock that Sheldon has girl problems.

89
00:04:01,890 --> 00:04:03,790
No, Leonard, go ahead and mock.

90
00:04:03,790 --> 00:04:05,280
Like my daddy always said,

91
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:09,690
"Shelly, women aren't anything but flippin' pains in the bottom."

92
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:13,890
That's what your father used to say?

93
00:04:14,130 --> 00:04:16,380
Well, I took out the bad words and the yeehaw,

94
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:17,970
but you get the gist.

95
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:21,660
Look, if you don't want to go to the party, just don't go.

96
00:04:21,660 --> 00:04:23,080
You're a grown man.

97
00:04:23,080 --> 00:04:24,360
Act like one.

98
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:26,430
Tell Amy you want to spend the weekend having a sleepover

99
00:04:26,430 --> 00:04:28,710
and playing video games with your friends.

100
00:04:30,330 --> 00:04:31,600
Maybe she'll dig it.

101
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:34,270
Women like a firm hand on the tiller.

102
00:04:34,770 --> 00:04:36,510
I can never find the tiller.

103
00:04:39,510 --> 00:04:41,660
I got a book; it didn't help.

104
00:04:43,090 --> 00:04:45,460
Yeah, I always thought if I were ever enslaved,

105
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:49,040
it would be by an advanced species from another planet,

106
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:51,530
not some hotsy-totsy from Glendale.

107
00:04:52,980 --> 00:04:54,800
Now, I downloaded an app that

108
00:04:54,800 --> 00:04:58,000
might be helpful in this situation.

109
00:05:03,200 --> 00:05:04,460
You're right.

110
00:05:04,700 --> 00:05:05,710
I'm smart as a whip.

111
00:05:05,710 --> 00:05:07,180
I should be able to figure this out.

112
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:12,700
Hey, listen, I kind of made plans

113
00:05:12,700 --> 00:05:14,870
with the guys this weekend, but then I wondered,

114
00:05:14,870 --> 00:05:16,950
because we're in this relationship-beta-test,

115
00:05:16,950 --> 00:05:19,310
if I should have asked you first.

116
00:05:19,310 --> 00:05:21,980
Then I thought if I did check with you first,

117
00:05:21,980 --> 00:05:24,920
then you'd think that I was taking things to seriously.

118
00:05:24,920 --> 00:05:27,230
And then-en I got a nosebleed.

119
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:30,740
You don't have to check with me.

120
00:05:30,740 --> 00:05:32,220
Do whatever you want.

121
00:05:33,830 --> 00:05:36,840
I guess I was hoping for a different reaction, but okay.

122
00:05:36,990 --> 00:05:38,880
Really, what were you hoping for?

123
00:05:38,880 --> 00:05:39,900
I don't know,

124
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:42,290
maybe that you'd be a little upset,

125
00:05:42,290 --> 00:05:43,790
and then you'd realize that

126
00:05:43,790 --> 00:05:46,300
I'm a stallion that has to run free.

127
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:52,320
And that would turn you on a little.

128
00:05:53,250 --> 00:05:55,610
Okay, I'm an actress. Ask me again.

129
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:58,630
Do you mind if I spend the weekend

130
00:05:58,630 --> 00:06:00,390
playing video games with the guys?

131
00:06:00,390 --> 00:06:02,140
Wha... the entire weekend?

132
00:06:02,150 --> 00:06:03,930
You mean I wouldn't see you at all?

133
00:06:03,930 --> 00:06:04,820
But I j...

134
00:06:04,820 --> 00:06:05,730
No, no...

135
00:06:05,730 --> 00:06:07,940
I knew what I was getting into.

136
00:06:09,370 --> 00:06:12,080
You can't put a saddle on Leonard Hofstadter.

137
00:06:13,620 --> 00:06:16,230
Oh, my, is it getting hot in here?

138
00:06:16,230 --> 00:06:17,850
Ay, papi.

139
00:06:19,450 --> 00:06:21,080
Ay, papi?

140
00:06:22,080 --> 00:06:23,250
What is that?

141
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:25,300
An acting choice.

142
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:27,680
So you chose that when you become turned on,

143
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:30,410
you turn into Speedy Gonzalez?

144
00:06:32,050 --> 00:06:34,180
Choo got a problem with that, papi?

145
00:06:37,200 --> 00:06:40,500
Penny! Penny! Penny!

146
00:06:40,800 --> 00:06:41,940
Sorry, Stallion.

147
00:06:41,940 --> 00:06:44,160
Your weird friend Giraffe is here.

148
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:47,550
Hello, Penny!

149
00:06:47,550 --> 00:06:50,540
I just stopped by to bring you this gift.

150
00:06:50,550 --> 00:06:52,200
Gummy bears? Thank you.

151
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:54,160
Now that you're in my debt...

152
00:06:55,470 --> 00:06:57,890
...please manipulate Amy into releasing me

153
00:06:57,890 --> 00:07:01,220
from my commitment to attend her aunt's tedious birthday party.

154
00:07:02,390 --> 00:07:03,160
Not a chance.

155
00:07:03,160 --> 00:07:04,330
All right.

156
00:07:04,330 --> 00:07:05,880
I thought the candy might not be enough

157
00:07:05,880 --> 00:07:07,660
so let me up the ante.

158
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:10,490
These are Cooper Coupons.

159
00:07:10,490 --> 00:07:13,450
These are for various things I can do for you.

160
00:07:13,450 --> 00:07:14,640
Um, oh, this one

161
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:17,550
is for one free grammar check.

162
00:07:18,360 --> 00:07:20,780
You could use it for emails, letters,

163
00:07:20,790 --> 00:07:22,510
tattoos, what have you.

164
00:07:23,400 --> 00:07:24,680
Oh, this is fun one!

165
00:07:24,680 --> 00:07:28,500
This is an afternoon with me at the California Science Center,

166
00:07:28,500 --> 00:07:30,900
where I point out their mistakes.

167
00:07:32,580 --> 00:07:34,140
Keep an eye on those expiration dates,

168
00:07:34,140 --> 00:07:36,170
I've been burned more than once.

169
00:07:37,790 --> 00:07:38,960
All right, sweetie, I'm not going to get involved

170
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:40,110
in your relationship.

171
00:07:40,110 --> 00:07:42,300
Oh, come on. It's just a simple favor.

172
00:07:42,300 --> 00:07:43,520
Now, when's the last time I asked you

173
00:07:43,520 --> 00:07:45,070
to do something for me?

174
00:07:45,150 --> 00:07:46,620
Yesterday. You made me look in your ear

175
00:07:46,620 --> 00:07:48,800
to see if there was a ladybug in it.

176
00:07:49,920 --> 00:07:51,430
When is the last time I asked you to do something

177
00:07:51,430 --> 00:07:53,330
that wasn't a medical emergency?

178
00:07:53,330 --> 00:07:54,680
Yesterday. You made me look in your ear

179
00:07:54,690 --> 00:07:56,890
to see if there was a ladybug in it.

180
00:07:58,370 --> 00:07:59,570
All right, then, I have no choice

181
00:07:59,570 --> 00:08:01,270
but to go on to plan B.

182
00:08:01,270 --> 00:08:01,950
What's that?

183
00:08:01,950 --> 00:08:02,830
I'm going to run around outside

184
00:08:02,830 --> 00:08:04,940
with a wet head and try to catch a cold.

185
00:08:09,790 --> 00:08:10,680
Good morning.

186
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:11,860
Hello.

187
00:08:12,610 --> 00:08:14,740
I think you're really going to enjoy yourself today.

188
00:08:14,810 --> 00:08:16,630
Not only do you get to meet my relatives,

189
00:08:16,630 --> 00:08:18,860
but since my aunt's nursing home is catering the party,

190
00:08:18,860 --> 00:08:20,430
all of the food is incredibly soft.

191
00:08:20,430 --> 00:08:22,310
It's like a vacation for your teeth.

192
00:08:22,910 --> 00:08:24,000
All right.

193
00:08:26,360 --> 00:08:27,880
You sure you're okay with this?

194
00:08:27,940 --> 00:08:29,030
Yes.

195
00:08:29,030 --> 00:08:30,740
I decided to find a way

196
00:08:30,740 --> 00:08:34,440
that I could have this experience and enjoy it.

197
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:36,660
Thank you. That means a lot to me.

198
00:08:36,670 --> 00:08:38,010
Oh, don't thank me.

199
00:08:38,010 --> 00:08:39,820
Thank wireless technology.

200
00:08:39,820 --> 00:08:42,970
I realized, I can go to your aunt's awful party

201
00:08:42,970 --> 00:08:46,660
and still spend the whole day gaming with my friends.

202
00:08:48,560 --> 00:08:50,610
Sheldon, my relatives are going to want to talk to you,

203
00:08:50,610 --> 00:08:52,760
and you're going to be sitting there playing a game?

204
00:08:52,760 --> 00:08:54,520
Isn't that a little rude?

205
00:08:54,530 --> 00:08:56,510
Oh, I got that covered.

206
00:08:57,260 --> 00:08:58,220
Headset.

207
00:08:58,220 --> 00:09:00,670
I won't hear a word the old geezers are saying.

208
00:09:04,140 --> 00:09:06,320
You know, if playing that game is more important to you

209
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:07,550
than honoring your commitment to me,

210
00:09:07,550 --> 00:09:10,130
and you don't mind me showing up at a party all by myself

211
00:09:10,130 --> 00:09:12,340
after I've already told everybody I'll be bringing somebody,

212
00:09:12,340 --> 00:09:13,940
then, fine.

213
00:09:13,960 --> 00:09:15,580
Go home and play your game.

214
00:09:17,870 --> 00:09:19,090
Thanks.

215
00:09:20,870 --> 00:09:22,100
Ooh, listen,

216
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:25,110
I wouldn't mind a piece of birthday cake,

217
00:09:25,110 --> 00:09:28,840
provided the old gal's candle blow is clean and dry.

218
00:09:36,930 --> 00:09:38,390
Here you go.

219
00:09:38,390 --> 00:09:41,190
I've got everything we'll need for the big game:

220
00:09:41,190 --> 00:09:43,330
low-fat turkey jerky...

221
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:46,530
low-carb beer...

222
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:50,020
100-calorie snack pack...

223
00:09:50,910 --> 00:09:52,420
You pick up a Y chromosome while you were there?

224
00:09:52,420 --> 00:09:54,010
You might be short one.

225
00:09:54,940 --> 00:09:56,810
Hey, I plan on leveling up in the game,

226
00:09:56,810 --> 00:09:59,580
not my swimsuit size, thank you very much.

227
00:10:00,060 --> 00:10:02,120
Gentlemen, the game offers us a choice,

228
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:05,050
between playing for the Republic and the light side,

229
00:10:05,050 --> 00:10:08,140
or the Sith Empire and the dark side.

230
00:10:08,140 --> 00:10:09,510
Well, we're always the good guys.

231
00:10:09,510 --> 00:10:10,880
In D&D, we're lawful good,

232
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:12,800
in City Of Heroes, we're the heroes,

233
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:13,980
and Grand Theft Auto,

234
00:10:13,980 --> 00:10:15,560
we pay the prostitutes promptly,

235
00:10:15,560 --> 00:10:17,310
and never hit them with a bat.

236
00:10:20,850 --> 00:10:22,800
Those women are prostitutes?

237
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:27,360
You said they were raising money for stem cell research.

238
00:10:29,620 --> 00:10:31,710
Hey, guys, I got a surprise.

239
00:10:31,710 --> 00:10:33,440
Hm, if it's yogurt that helps ladies poop,

240
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:35,400
I think Raj beat you to it.

241
00:10:37,020 --> 00:10:39,480
No. Bernadette's going to be playing with us.

242
00:10:39,480 --> 00:10:42,840
So, that's pretty cool, huh? Right? Sure it is, yeah.

243
00:10:43,890 --> 00:10:45,810
What, you invited your girlfriend?!

244
00:10:45,810 --> 00:10:48,100
This is supposed to be our weekend!

245
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:50,100
I had no choice. Last night, she said,

246
00:10:50,100 --> 00:10:51,450
"Why don't we go out for brunch tomorrow

247
00:10:51,450 --> 00:10:52,720
and then maybe the Arboretum."

248
00:10:52,720 --> 00:10:53,820
And I said, "Well, no,

249
00:10:53,820 --> 00:10:54,880
I promised the guys I was going to

250
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:56,240
play a video game with them all weekend."

251
00:10:56,240 --> 00:10:57,470
And she said, "That sounds like fun.

252
00:10:57,470 --> 00:10:58,180
Can I come, too?"

253
00:10:58,180 --> 00:11:00,230
And then I didn't answer for a second, and then she said,

254
00:11:00,230 --> 00:11:01,550
"Well, do you not want me to come?"

255
00:11:01,550 --> 00:11:03,110
And then I bought her a new laptop and the game,

256
00:11:03,110 --> 00:11:04,930
and she's parking the car right now.

257
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:08,910
Is the whip sound app

258
00:11:08,910 --> 00:11:10,560
contextually appropriate here?

259
00:11:10,560 --> 00:11:14,040
Uh, it is, but I think you might've waited too long

260
00:11:14,040 --> 00:11:15,740
for it to be funny.

261
00:11:20,570 --> 00:11:21,960
I was wrong; it's still funny.

262
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:23,210
Oh, good.

263
00:11:31,270 --> 00:11:32,920
Amy, what's wrong?

264
00:11:32,970 --> 00:11:34,660
My boyfriend's a jerk.

265
00:11:35,770 --> 00:11:37,330
Well, I know he didn't cheat on you,

266
00:11:37,330 --> 00:11:38,750
so what happened?

267
00:11:40,760 --> 00:11:42,720
I had to go to my aunt's party all by myself,

268
00:11:42,720 --> 00:11:44,090
and everybody was like,

269
00:11:44,090 --> 00:11:45,680
"Where's this boyfriend you're always talking about?

270
00:11:45,680 --> 00:11:47,480
"Is he real, or did you make him up like Armen,

271
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:49,340
the miniature horse breeder?"

272
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:53,980
Who's Armen the miniature horse breeder?

273
00:11:53,980 --> 00:11:57,390
The pretend boyfriend I invented to get my family off my back.

274
00:11:57,470 --> 00:11:59,370
It unraveled quickly when I couldn't answer the question

275
00:11:59,370 --> 00:12:00,910
"How'd you two meet?"

276
00:12:02,700 --> 00:12:04,600
I would have thought at a miniature horse show.

277
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:05,920
Oh, that's good.

278
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:10,220
I panicked and said Woodstock.

279
00:12:11,950 --> 00:12:14,390
I just wanted to show Sheldon off to my family.

280
00:12:14,730 --> 00:12:15,920
Sure, I get that.

281
00:12:15,920 --> 00:12:17,860
I mean, he's your first boyfriend and all.

282
00:12:17,860 --> 00:12:20,070
Not just my first boyfriend, he's the best boyfriend.

283
00:12:20,070 --> 00:12:21,910
I mean, think about it.

284
00:12:21,910 --> 00:12:24,170
I'm dating Sheldon Cooper.

285
00:12:27,070 --> 00:12:27,630
Yes.

286
00:12:27,630 --> 00:12:29,060
On purpose.

287
00:12:30,340 --> 00:12:32,130
He's handsome, he's lanky,

288
00:12:32,130 --> 00:12:33,660
he's brilliant,

289
00:12:33,660 --> 00:12:36,600
and his skin has that pale, waxy quality.

290
00:12:37,750 --> 00:12:40,320
Well, sickly is the new sexy.

291
00:12:42,970 --> 00:12:44,480
Yeah.

292
00:12:45,980 --> 00:12:47,020
You know, Amy,

293
00:12:47,020 --> 00:12:49,140
sometimes when you're in a relationship with someone

294
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:51,430
you really care about, the sucky part is,

295
00:12:51,430 --> 00:12:53,390
it leaves you open to getting hurt.

296
00:12:53,960 --> 00:12:56,080
Do you ever worry about Leonard doing that to you?

297
00:12:56,520 --> 00:12:58,470
That's hilarious. No.

298
00:13:00,950 --> 00:13:02,580
Get that guy! Get that guy!

299
00:13:06,180 --> 00:13:07,280
Dr. Rostenkowski,

300
00:13:07,280 --> 00:13:08,730
it may interest you to know

301
00:13:08,730 --> 00:13:11,560
that saying "Pew, pew, pew" isn't as effective

302
00:13:11,560 --> 00:13:13,950
as pressing your blaster key.

303
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:15,820
In the same way that saying "Whee!"

304
00:13:15,820 --> 00:13:18,130
doesn't make the land speeder go.

305
00:13:23,330 --> 00:13:25,600
Raj, Imperial Troopers on your tail.

306
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:27,250
Got him.

307
00:13:27,250 --> 00:13:30,170
When Gandhi advocated his philosophy of non-violence,

308
00:13:30,170 --> 00:13:33,180
I bet he didn't know how much fun it was killing stuff.

309
00:13:34,870 --> 00:13:36,630
All right, I think we got them all.

310
00:13:36,630 --> 00:13:38,140
Let's divide up the loot.

311
00:13:38,140 --> 00:13:40,860
Ooh, look at this pretty purple robe I just got.

312
00:13:40,860 --> 00:13:43,210
You should put on yours and then we'll match.

313
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:45,790
But I worked hard to get this armor.

314
00:13:46,330 --> 00:13:47,400
Sorry, I just thought it'd be nice

315
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:49,530
if people knew we were a couple.

316
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:52,740
Fine, I'll change.

317
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:08,600
- I don't think I want to play a game. - Oh, come on!

318
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:10,900
They're playing one across the hall-- we should, too.

319
00:14:10,900 --> 00:14:14,090
Okay, we are gonna take turns bouncing a quarter

320
00:14:14,090 --> 00:14:16,050
off the table, and if it goes into this cup,

321
00:14:16,050 --> 00:14:17,510
the other person has to drink.

322
00:14:17,510 --> 00:14:19,020
Then you get to go again...

323
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:25,190
Like that?

324
00:14:25,620 --> 00:14:27,510
Wow. Yeah, b-beginner's luck.

325
00:14:27,510 --> 00:14:30,240
So, now I will drink this entire cup of beer,

326
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:32,190
and you will go again...

327
00:14:36,650 --> 00:14:37,300
All right.

328
00:14:37,300 --> 00:14:40,170
So, yeah, okay, now I'm gonna drink this entire cup

329
00:14:40,170 --> 00:14:42,660
and then I'm going to drink another one.

330
00:14:42,690 --> 00:14:44,740
Okay, seriously, stop. What the hell?

331
00:14:46,440 --> 00:14:47,390
Spent a lot of my childhood

332
00:14:47,390 --> 00:14:50,000
throwing coins into wishing wells hoping for friends.

333
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,330
At a certain point, you start doing trick shots

334
00:14:51,330 --> 00:14:53,030
just to keep things interesting.

335
00:14:53,970 --> 00:14:56,390
Whoa, give me a second to catch up here. Hold on.

336
00:14:59,160 --> 00:15:00,770
That'd be my boyfriend

337
00:15:00,820 --> 00:15:03,190
happier playing his dopey Star Trek game with his friends

338
00:15:03,190 --> 00:15:04,550
than hanging out with me.

339
00:15:04,550 --> 00:15:06,850
- Wars. - What?

340
00:15:07,270 --> 00:15:07,870
Star Wars.

341
00:15:07,870 --> 00:15:10,120
They get all cranky when you mix the two up.

342
00:15:10,400 --> 00:15:11,240
What's the difference?

343
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:13,650
There's absolutely no difference.

344
00:15:16,320 --> 00:15:18,400
How do I get him to treat me better?

345
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:19,890
All right.

346
00:15:19,890 --> 00:15:22,030
Let me give you a little girlfriend 101.

347
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:24,490
Usually the first move out of the gate

348
00:15:24,490 --> 00:15:25,420
is you withhold sex,

349
00:15:25,420 --> 00:15:28,500
but that will work better after Sheldon hits puberty.

350
00:15:28,570 --> 00:15:31,770
So, I'd say...

351
00:15:31,770 --> 00:15:33,690
give him the silent treatment.

352
00:15:33,930 --> 00:15:36,020
No, he loves that.

353
00:15:36,230 --> 00:15:37,600
Our record for sitting in a room together

354
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:40,410
and not speaking to each other is six-and-a half hours.

355
00:15:40,420 --> 00:15:42,280
He said it was a magical evening.

356
00:15:43,420 --> 00:15:45,000
All right, then we're gonna have to go

357
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:46,340
with an oldie but goodie;

358
00:15:46,350 --> 00:15:48,000
making a scene.

359
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:49,490
I don't think I'd be good at that.

360
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:50,840
That's why you're lucky to have me.

361
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:52,520
Back in Omaha, there are two different restaurants

362
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:55,200
I'm not allowed into. Both Chili's.

363
00:15:59,260 --> 00:16:02,080
Bernadette, remember, your character's the healer in our group.

364
00:16:02,080 --> 00:16:05,010
You're in charge of healing all of us, not just Howard.

365
00:16:05,010 --> 00:16:06,370
I can't help it.

366
00:16:06,370 --> 00:16:08,920
My Howie Wowie has an owie.

367
00:16:11,120 --> 00:16:12,980
That is the most sickeningly sweet thing

368
00:16:12,980 --> 00:16:15,310
I have ever experienced.

369
00:16:15,350 --> 00:16:18,390
And I am sipping Kool-Aid through a Red Vine.

370
00:16:21,670 --> 00:16:24,120
Sheldon Cooper, I've got a bone to pick with you,

371
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:25,950
and I'm about to do it in front of all your friends.

372
00:16:25,950 --> 00:16:28,560
Yeah, you pick that bone. You pick that bone clean!

373
00:16:29,630 --> 00:16:31,060
I'm gonna publicly shame you,

374
00:16:31,060 --> 00:16:32,700
and then sit back as societal pressure

375
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,620
compels you to modify your behavior.

376
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:37,240
Ooh, buuurn!

377
00:16:38,490 --> 00:16:40,150
And if you don't start treating me better,

378
00:16:40,150 --> 00:16:40,760
I'm leaving you

379
00:16:40,760 --> 00:16:43,140
for a miniature horse breeder named Armen.

380
00:16:45,610 --> 00:16:46,550
Armen who?

381
00:16:46,550 --> 00:16:48,600
Armen... damn it.

382
00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:53,920
Look, Sheldon, she wanted to show you off to her family,

383
00:16:53,920 --> 00:16:55,580
and you stood her up, okay?

384
00:16:55,870 --> 00:16:58,270
Look at this adorable, smushy face.

385
00:16:58,270 --> 00:17:00,600
Smush, smush, smush.

386
00:17:01,760 --> 00:17:02,680
You're hurting me.

387
00:17:02,680 --> 00:17:05,790
No, Sheldon hurt you.

388
00:17:06,260 --> 00:17:08,110
Before; now it's you.

389
00:17:10,230 --> 00:17:12,690
I think I understand.

390
00:17:12,850 --> 00:17:13,830
You're the one person

391
00:17:13,830 --> 00:17:16,620
who can say Sheldon Cooper is your boyfriend,

392
00:17:16,630 --> 00:17:18,010
but that rings hollow

393
00:17:18,010 --> 00:17:20,770
if you can't lord him over others in the flesh.

394
00:17:22,100 --> 00:17:23,990
I forget what I bring to the party

395
00:17:23,990 --> 00:17:26,150
and what I take away when I leave.

396
00:17:27,560 --> 00:17:31,810
Please accept these valuable Cooper Coupons...

397
00:17:34,390 --> 00:17:35,760
...as restitution.

398
00:17:35,760 --> 00:17:37,410
Sheldon, she doesn't want your stupid...

399
00:17:37,410 --> 00:17:39,060
Ooh, Science Center. Redeeming.

400
00:17:39,060 --> 00:17:40,030
Let's go.

401
00:17:42,500 --> 00:17:44,380
Well played, Amy Farrah Fowler.

402
00:17:44,380 --> 00:17:46,030
Let me get my coat.

403
00:17:47,650 --> 00:17:49,390
Oh, grow up, Leonard.

404
00:17:51,010 --> 00:17:52,150
But e-excuse me,

405
00:17:52,150 --> 00:17:53,830
I have something to say.

406
00:17:55,210 --> 00:17:57,290
None of you may realize it,

407
00:17:57,290 --> 00:17:59,780
but I was very much looking forward to this weekend.

408
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:01,350
It was gonna be like the old days--

409
00:18:01,350 --> 00:18:03,890
the four of us hanging out playing video games

410
00:18:03,890 --> 00:18:06,860
before you guys all got girlfriends.

411
00:18:07,210 --> 00:18:08,100
Do you have any idea what it's like

412
00:18:08,100 --> 00:18:11,170
to be the only one without a girlfriend?

413
00:18:11,170 --> 00:18:12,640
Even if I get one someday,

414
00:18:12,640 --> 00:18:17,020
I'll still be the guy who got a girl after Sheldon Cooper!

415
00:18:21,920 --> 00:18:24,520
And that's how a girl makes a scene.

416
00:18:29,730 --> 00:18:30,400
I'm sorry, sweetie.

417
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:32,050
You're right. You deserve your weekend.

418
00:18:32,050 --> 00:18:33,280
Come on, Amy, let's go.

419
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:34,880
What about the Science Center?

420
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:37,250
I'll let you hold my hair while I throw up.

421
00:18:39,490 --> 00:18:40,740
Rain check.

422
00:18:42,270 --> 00:18:43,560
I'm gonna go, too.

423
00:18:43,560 --> 00:18:45,440
- I'll miss you. - I'll miss you.

424
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:46,870
- I'll miss you more. - No, I'll...

425
00:18:46,870 --> 00:18:48,540
Just leave!

426
00:18:52,850 --> 00:18:54,060
Okay, now.

427
00:18:54,450 --> 00:18:56,010
This is the way it's supposed to be.

428
00:18:56,370 --> 00:18:58,890
Men together, fighting the forces of evil.

429
00:18:58,960 --> 00:19:00,300
Hear! Hear!

430
00:19:03,140 --> 00:19:05,640
I can't believe this is only 64 calories.

431
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:21,960
Howard Joel Wolowitz!

432
00:19:21,970 --> 00:19:23,740
I've been worried sick for two days,

433
00:19:23,740 --> 00:19:26,260
and I know you turned off your phone!

434
00:19:28,810 --> 00:19:30,490
You open up this door right now

435
00:19:30,490 --> 00:19:32,480
because I've had it up to here!

436
00:19:32,480 --> 00:19:34,580
I have been to the morgue and the hospital,

437
00:19:34,580 --> 00:19:36,320
and I spent the last half hour

438
00:19:36,330 --> 00:19:39,220
walking up these ferkakta stairs!

439
00:19:42,340 --> 00:19:44,030
That's my ride; got to go.

